    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Seeing as bfloat16 works I suspect that you might just be running out of range since float16's max normal value is 65504\r\n\r\n```Python\r\n# lets see initial of q\r\nprint(f\"ABS MAX Q: {q.abs().max()}\")\r\nprint(f\"ABS MAX K: {k.abs().max()}\")\r\noutput = torch.matmul(q, k.transpose(-2, -1))\r\nprint(f\"Output has NaN: {torch.isnan(output).any()} Output has Inf {torch.isinf(output).any()}\")\r\n\r\n# lets see what the max dot_prod is\r\nq_hp = q.to(torch.float32)\r\nk_hp = k.to(torch.float32)\r\n\r\noutput_hp = torch.matmul(q_hp, k_hp.transpose(-2, -1))\r\nprint(f\"Max dot_prod = {output_hp.abs().max()}\")\r\n```\r\nProduces:\r\n``` Shell\r\nABS MAX Q: 576.0\r\nABS MAX K: 382.75\r\nOutput has NaN: False Output has Inf True\r\nMax dot_prod = 784449.375\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe reason why this doesn't fail with the fused kernel is that the accumulator is using high precision and thus can store the intermediates\r\n ",
