    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "```Python\r\nimport torch\r\n\r\na = torch.full((1024, 1024), 350, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"cuda\")\r\nb = torch.full((1024, 1024), 350, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"cuda\")\r\n\r\nwith torch.autocast(\"cuda\", torch.float16):\r\n    c = a @ b\r\n    print(f\"Abs max of c: {c.abs().max()}\")\r\n\r\nc_new = a @ b\r\nprint(f\"Abs max no autocast: {c_new.abs().max()}\")\r\n```\r\n```Shell\r\nAbs max of c: inf\r\nAbs max no autocast: 125438096.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile the accumulator during the matmul might be in fp32 the output of it will be the autocasted type AFAIK and this conversion will saturate fp16 and cause the infs",
